I now have a complete, concrete profile. Here is the analysis.

---

# SASS instruction-mix profile — paged-prefill kernel (USE_TMA=0, COOP cp.async)

**Binary:** `/home/yak/fa3-cuda/.fa3_trials/nofence/nofence.so`
**Arch:** `sm_90a` (compiled with CUDA 13.0 toolkit)
**Symbol (text section 227):**
`_ZN2pf14prefill_kernelI13__nv_bfloat16S1_Li128ELi128ELb0ELb0ELi3ELi128ELi128ELi1E...`
= `pf::prefill_kernel<__nv_bfloat16, __nv_bfloat16, 128, 128, 0, 0, 3, 128, 128, 1>`

Template args map to: Bq=128, Bkv=128, USE_TMA=0, (flag)=0, **NSTAGE=3**, Dqk=128, Dv=128, ... . Confirmed **no `UTMALDG` anywhere** — this instantiation is pure COOP cp.async gather (as expected for paged KV with USE_TMA=0). The kernel is warp-specialized: a **producer** warpgroup (cp.async gather) and **consumer** math warpgroups.

## Control-flow skeleton (back-edges detected)
- **Consumer mainloop:** `0x3fe0` → back-edge `@!P0 BRA 0x3fe0` at **`0x7020`**.
- **Producer COOP loop:** `0xbd70` → back-edge `@!P0 BRA 0xbd70` at **`0xd8f0`**.
- mbarrier wait-spin trampolines live at `0xe7f0–0xe8d0`.
- Pipeline depth 3 confirmed by mbarrier init: 7× `SYNCS.EXCH.64` at smem offsets `0x38000/8/10` (full) + `0x38018/20/28` (empty) + `0x38030` (cp.async LDGSTSBAR).

---

## A. CONSUMER steady-state mainloop `[0x3fe0 … 0x7020]`

Structure per iteration is the classic FA3 pipelined order: **QK MMA → PV MMA (of previous P) → softmax(current S)**, with a causal/boundary mask block that is **branch-skipped in the steady state** (`@P0 BRA P1, 0x5720` at `0x4900` jumps over a 64×`FSEL` mask block `0x4910–0x5710`).

### Per-iteration instruction MIX (steady-state, interior/non-masked path)

| Op | Count | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| **HGMMA.64x128x16.F32.BF16** | **8** | S = Q·Kᵀ; K-depth 128 = 8×16; accum R24 |
| **HGMMA.64x64x16.F32.BF16 .tnspB** | **16** | O += P·V; transposed-B; 2 N-halves (accum R88 ×8, R120 ×8) → head_dim 128 = 2×64, K-depth 128 = 8×16 |
| **MUFU.EX2** | **66** | softmax exp2 (64 P-elems/thread + 2 running-stat) |
| **F2FP.BF16.F32.PACK_AB** | **32** | P: F32→BF16 pack, feeds next PV HGMMA A-operand |
| **FMNMX.FTZ** | **76** | row-max reduction tree + running-max update |
| **FADD.FTZ** | **72** | row-sum accumulation |
| **FMUL.FTZ** | **68** | scaling |
| **FFMA.FTZ** | **66** | exp2 arg fuse + O rescale by correction factor |
| **SHFL.BFLY** | **4** | cross-lane row-max/row-sum reduce (offsets 0x1, 0x2) |
| **WARPGROUP.ARRIVE** | **2** | one before QK block, one before PV block |
| **WARPGROUP.DEPBAR.LE gsb0** | **2** | scoreboard waits (`,0x1` after QK; `,0x0` before softmax) |
| **BAR.SYNC.DEFER_BLOCKING R18, 0x100** | **1** | named barrier (dyn ID R18, 256 thr) — WG↔WG ping-pong sync, loop head |
| **BAR.ARV R9, 0x100** | **1** | named-barrier arrive (dyn ID R9, 256 thr) |
| **SYNCS.PHASECHK.TRANS64.TRYWAIT** | **1** | mbarrier try_wait on K/V tile-ready |
| **SYNCS.ARRIVE.TRANS64.A1T0** | **1** | mbarrier arrive → release consumed buffer to producer |
| **WARPSYNC.ALL** | **1** | |
| **LDGSTS / LDSM / LDS / STS** | **0** | none — HGMMA operands read directly from smem via GMMA descriptors `gdesc[UR..]` |

**HGMMA total = 24/iter** (8 QK + 16 PV). No `LDSM`/`LDS` in the mainloop — this is the descriptor-based (`gdesc`) GMMA path, so there are zero shared-mem operand loads on the consumer side.

### Issue order / interleave (representative)

QK block — 8 back-to-back `HGMMA.64x128x16`, each interleaved with uniform-register descriptor bumps for the next tile, bracketed by `WARPGROUP.ARRIVE` / scoreboard:
```
/*4160*/  WARPGROUP.ARRIVE ;
/*4230*/  HGMMA.64x128x16.F32.BF16 R24, gdesc[UR20], RZ, !UPT ;   // first: no accum
/*4300*/  HGMMA.64x128x16.F32.BF16 R24, gdesc[UR20], R24 ;        // +6 more, accumulate
/*4590*/  HGMMA.64x128x16.F32.BF16 R24, gdesc[UR20], R24, gsb0 ;  // last tagged to scoreboard gsb0
```
PV block — 16 back-to-back `HGMMA.64x64x16 .tnspB`, two accumulator groups (R88, then R120):
```
/*45a0*/  WARPGROUP.ARRIVE ;
/*45b0*/  HGMMA.64x64x16.F32.BF16 R88, R172, gdesc[UR16].tnspB, R88 ;   // ×8 into R88
/*4730*/  HGMMA.64x64x16.F32.BF16 R120, R172, gdesc[UR16].tnspB, R120 ; // ×8 into R120
/*48a0*/  HGMMA.64x64x16.F32.BF16 R120, R180, gdesc[UR16].tnspB, R120, gsb0 ;
/*48c0*/  BAR.ARV R9, 0x100 ;
/*48e0*/  WARPGROUP.DEPBAR.LE gsb0, 0x1 ;
/*4900*/  @P0 BRA P1, 0x5720 ;        // steady state: skip the 64×FSEL mask block
```
Softmax block `0x5720–0x7020` — row-max reduction is an `FMNMX.FTZ` tree over the in-register S tile, then `SHFL.BFLY` combine:
```
/*5730*/  FMNMX.FTZ R17, R24, -INF , !PT ;   // ... long FMNMX reduction chain ...
/*59d0*/  SHFL.BFLY PT, R10, R19, 0x1, 0x1f ;
/*5a60*/  SHFL.BFLY PT, R17, R16, 0x2, 0x1f ;
```
exp + sum + P-pack, tightly interleaved (exp2 arg fused as `S*scale − rowmax` in one FFMA; `UR10 = scale·log2e`, `R10 = rowmax·scale`):
```
/*5c80*/  FFMA.FTZ R25, R25, UR10, -R10.reuse ;   // exp2 argument (fused scale + max-subtract)
/*5cd0*/  MUFU.EX2 R24, R24 ;                      // exp2
/*5ee0*/  FADD.FTZ R10, RZ, R25 ;                  // row-sum accumulate
/*5ef0*/  F2FP.BF16.F32.PACK_AB R172, R25, R24 ;   // pack P → BF16 for next PV HGMMA
```

The two mbarrier events per iter: consumer **waits** tile-ready via `SYNCS.PHASECHK.TRANS64.TRYWAIT P0,[R17+0x38000]` (`0x40c0`) and **releases** the buffer via `SYNCS.ARRIVE.TRANS64.A1T0 RZ,[UR16+0x38018]` (`0x57f0`). Named barriers use **dynamic IDs** (registers R18/R9, count `0x100`=256), i.e. warpgroup-relative ping-pong barriers, not literal IDs.

