## B. COOP PRODUCER loop `[0xbd70 … 0xd8f0]` (cp.async gather)

Per-iteration MIX (one pipeline stage = K tile + V tile):

| Op | Count | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| **LDGSTS.E.BYPASS.128** | **32** | cp.async, **16-byte**, **BYPASS = L1-bypass / CG (cache-global streaming) hint**; issued predicated `@P0/@P1` in groups of 4 |
| **STS.128 (…RZ)** | 32 | predicated `@!P0` **zero-fill** of smem for out-of-bounds rows (paired 1:1 with the gathered rows) |
| **LDS** | 48 | all `@!PT` (dead/predicated-off placeholders) — not executed |
| **LDG.E.CONSTANT** + **LDC.64 c[0x0][0x218]** | 1 + | page-table / block-index gather for paged KV |
| **SYNCS.PHASECHK.TRANS64.TRYWAIT** | 1 | wait for empty (consumed) buffer |
| **ARRIVES.LDGSTSBAR.64.ARVCNT [UR7+0x38030]** | 1 | cp.async-group commit → mbarrier arrive (signals tile-ready) |
| **MUFU.RCP** | 1 | address/stride recip |
| HGMMA / MUFU.EX2 | 0 | none — pure loader |

Representative producer snippet (zero-fill vs. gather, then commit):
```
/*c3a0*/ @P0  LDC.64 R18, c[0x0][0x218] ;
/*c3b0*/ @!P0 STS.128 [R16+0x8000], RZ ;                              // OOB row → zero smem
/*c400*/ @P0  LDGSTS.E.BYPASS.128 [R16+0x8000],  desc[UR24][R36.64] ; // in-bounds → cp.async CG
/*c410*/ @P0  LDGSTS.E.BYPASS.128 [R16+0x20000], desc[UR24][R30.64] ;
...
/*d8a0*/      ARRIVES.LDGSTSBAR.64.ARVCNT [UR15+0x38000] ;            // commit group → arrive mbarrier
/*d8f0*/ @!P0 BRA 0xbd70 ;                                            // loop back
```
The single cache hint used for all KV loads is **`.BYPASS` (L1-bypass, cache-global/CG)** — there is no `.LTC`/L2-hint variant. Producer→consumer handshake is via `ARRIVES.LDGSTSBAR` (cp.async completion increments the tile-ready mbarrier); consumer→producer via `SYNCS.ARRIVE.TRANS64` (buffer-free).

